# Title: Process Execution From A Potentially Suspicious Folder
# ID: 3dfd06d2-eaf4-4532-9555-68aca59f57c4
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Tim Shelton
# Date: 2019-01-16
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1036
# Description: Detects a potentially suspicious execution from an uncommon folder.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((process_path="*:\\Perflogs\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Users\\All Users\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Users\\Default\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Users\\NetworkService\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Windows\\addins\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Windows\\debug\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Windows\\Fonts\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Windows\\Help\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Windows\\IME\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Windows\\Media\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Windows\\repair\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Windows\\security\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Windows\\System32\\Tasks\\*" OR process_path="*:\\Windows\\Tasks\\*" OR process_path="*$Recycle.bin*" OR process_path="*\\config\\systemprofile\\*" OR process_path="*\\Intel\\Logs\\*" OR process_path="*\\RSA\\MachineKeys\\*")) AND NOT (((process_path="C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\config\\systemprofile\\Citrix\\UpdaterBinaries\\*" AND process_path="*\\CitrixReceiverUpdater.exe") OR (process_path="C:\\Users\\Public\\IBM\\ClientSolutions\\Start_Programs\\*"))))
